<title>USA: Bombardier gets California commuter work.</title>
<headline>Bombardier gets California commuter work.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bombardier Transit Corp said Wednesday it was awarded a contract for the manufacture and supply of eight aluminum bi-level commuter railcars for the San Joaquin Regional Rail Commission in California.</p>
<p>The Bombardier Inc subsidiary said the contract is valued at $16 million.</p>
<p>The vehicles will be manufactured by Bombardier's Mass Transit Division at its Thunder Bay facility. Delivery is scheduled to begin in October 1997, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
